PRE-EXISTING, OUT-OF-SCOPE BLOCKER (documented, not a defect in this page)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The committed app target does not compile, independent of this page. Two distinct
pre-existing defects (both tracked at HEAD; `git ls-files` confirms; none modified
by this task) were introduced by prior parallel P4 widget/feature-view work:

(1) XCTest files compiled into the app product. 261 `*Tests.swift` files under the
    app-target source paths `TeslaSync/feature-views` + `TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets`
    `import XCTest` (+ `@testable import TeslaSync`). The first full build fails on the
    first of them:
      feature-views/AIRestorePanel.Tests.swift:18: error: unable to resolve module
      dependency: 'XCTest'
    (They belong in the XCTest bundle, not the app target.)

(2) Duplicate type declarations (parallel-collision). `public struct
    DashboardWidgetSize` (and `DashboardWidgetRegistration`) is declared in 16+ files
    that all compile into the one app module — e.g. BOTH
      Sources/DashboardWidgets/DrivetrainHealthWidgetModel.swift:10
      Sources/DashboardWidgets/BatteryCellsWidgetRegistry.swift:13
    (each commented "first native dashboard-widget surface"), plus 14 more under
    TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/*. Result:
      WallConnectorWidget.Model.swift:235: error: invalid redeclaration of 'DashboardWidgetSize'
      ...:251: error: 'DashboardWidgetSize' is ambiguous for type lookup ...
    Excluding the widget tier then surfaces a third cluster of duplicate-enum
    collisions across other feature-view surfaces (ElevationChart/FleetApiSection/...
    `cannot infer contextual base in reference to member 'loaded'/'live'/...`).

Fixing these requires de-duplicating shared primitives across hundreds of files from
other surfaces — explicitly out of scope for this single-page parity task ("Out of
Scope: other pages; new product features"). Crucially, ZERO of these errors are in
this page's files or in its sole dependency (FeatureToggles):
  $ grep -c 'Features/Admin/.*error:'         <build log>  → 0
  $ grep -c 'feature-views/FeatureToggles.*error:' <log>   → 0

